          <li><strong>For a Family or Group of 4:</strong> A larger rental vehicle (SUV or 7-seater minivan) runs €110–€150/day with insurance and fuel. A private Mercedes van or Toyota Prado from Roam Morocco runs €180–€220/day. The difference drops to just <strong>€15 to €20 per person per day</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Safety &amp; Road Realities: What You Must Know Before Driving</h2>
        <p>
          Morocco has poured billions of Dirhams into modernizing its national highway infrastructure over the past decade. The toll motorways (Autoroutes) connecting Tangier, Rabat, Casablanca, Marrakech, and Agadir are superb—four-lane divided expressways that rival French <em>autoroutes</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          However, most tourists do not come to Morocco to drive between Casablanca and Rabat. They come to explore the <strong>High Atlas Mountains</strong>, the ancient fortified kasbahs of Ouarzazate, the dramatic Dadès and Todra Gorges, and the rolling golden dunes of Erg Chebbi in Merzouga. And on those routes, the driving environment changes dramatically.
        </p>

        <!-- Image Callout -->
        <div style="margin: 36px 0; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 16px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.04); overflow: hidden;">
